{
  "requirement": "No prompt, tool result, or tool error the harness gives the model MUST state a\nline number or line range of a project source, except within source text it\nquotes and where a tool error repeats a line number the model supplied. The\nharness MUST identify a source location by file and outline selector under\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors` instead.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers` has these testable parts:\n\n1. No tool result states a line number or range of a project source.\n2. No tool error does, except where it repeats a number the model supplied.\n3. Nothing in a prompt does.\n4. Source locations are given as file plus outline selector, which `requirements.references.outline_selectors` defines. That requirement is cited as context only, so I did not reassess it.\n5. Source text the harness quotes is exempt.\n\n**Tool results.**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms]` checks the `habeas` item read and the line-range reads. It asserts there is no `line_start` or `line_end` field, only `item`.\n- `fn[line_range_reads_record_the_innermost_covering_nodes]` asserts the same for the `inputs` of line-range reads. It covers Rust and plain text, the nested node case, and the recorded inputs.\n- `fn[search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules]` and `fn[separate_windows_in_one_node_are_divided_by_an_elision_line]` cover `ripgrep`. They assert the entries and `lines` carry no `line_start` or `line` field, and the exact line objects hold only `text` and `matched`. Elision lines separate windows within a node.\n- `ast_grep` results go through the same `SearchNodes::entries` code, so the `ripgrep` assertions cover that path too.\n- `fn[outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs]` asserts the `outline` output has no line numbers.\n- `fn[references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs]` compares the whole `references` result by equality. It shows only a selector in `item`, with no lines.\n\n**Tool errors.**\n- The unit test `src/authoring/line_numbers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error]` checks `without_source_lines` directly. It covers the `line N:` prefix, the `file:N:` prefix, the `at line N, column M` suffix, and a second file position inside one message. Each is turned into `file#`. It also asserts that both forms of model-supplied position (single line and range, from `read_lines`) are kept unchanged.\n- The integration test `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_give_the_model_no_line_numbers_it_did_not_supply]` covers two end-to-end cases.\n  - A `line_start` far past the end of the file yields an error that repeats only the supplied start line.\n  - A genuine parse error from `habeas` does contain `line N: ` at dispatch, but the request actually delivered to the model does not.\n\n**Prompts.**\n- `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` checks the site prompt's match descriptions, which use kind, query and item with no lines. Alongside it, `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them]` asserts the exact `matches_value` JSON, which has no line fields.\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` asserts the exact mandatory-input objects, which contain only file, item, hash, kind and text.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[submission_description_tests]/fn[submission_descriptions_explain_arguments_and_successful_completion]` asserts the submission tool descriptions tell the model to use \"outline selectors\" and \"never line numbers\".\n\n**Residual points.** The model-facing mandatory inputs are not asserted directly through `model_mandatory_inputs`. The test compares `mandatory_inputs`, and `to_model_input` only adds kind and text to the recorded input, which has no line fields. I do not count this as a gap. Also, `without_source_lines` is tested on a representative set of diagnostic formats, not exhaustively. The requirement does not enumerate formats, so I do not treat that as a gap either.\n\nNo gap was found, and there are no acknowledgments to assess.",
  "references": "5f07d59d3d70ca6a503110d2a797133c2b9f1eafd54fb53e7ee2fb02587ec51a",
